{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-24 13:33:55 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-24 20:33:55 ICT\n\nVerdict: REJECTED\n\n- **CLOSED — r8 resource-lowering finding.** r9 directs stream handles and cursor cells into private `:resources`, remaps references without creating store keys, and adds an export round-trip test ([linker spec](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1403), [M4 test](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1895)).\n- **OPEN, P1 — Reference forgery remains unspecified.** r9 calls program-held references “unforgeable” while retaining IDs “exactly as a running program holds them” ([linker spec](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1415)). Today those references are ordinary maps with predictable IDs, and stream effects look up a handle using only the supplied `:id` ([ID minting](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:76), [reference creation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:172), [effect lookup](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:185)); the AST walker accepts a literal value as an effect target ([walker](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:296)). Moving the lookup to `:resources` alone would let a fabricated reference reach another resource. Specify an actually unforgeable, task-scoped reference and validation at every effect boundary; define its lift/lower remapping and test forged stream and cursor references, including FFI resource IDs.\n- **PARTIAL, P2 — Migration references.** Criterion 12 requires amendments to UCF 7.6.2, but the M4 file box still omits it ([criterion](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2008), [file box](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1944)). It also names “UCF 4.1,” which is not a section of the referenced UCF document ([UCF heading](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1)). Correct the reference and include every required amendment in M4.\n\nThe r9 file passes pure-ASCII and 80-column checks. **Consensus has not been reached; it is not ready to commit.**"}}
